se_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA (rebar-debug fast path; Step-7 sibling of 3d57-602f-0b75-48ee).\n\nMECHANISM (confirmed at runtime): child_closure_findings loops a parent's direct children and calls compute_validity(sig, c, 'completion-verifier') per closed child (src/rebar/llm/completion_child_gate.py). The completion branch (plan_review/attest.py:568-574) recomputes current_material_fingerprint -> live_material_children -> list_tickets(parent=...) -> reduce_all_tickets (1 full-store scan); a stale fingerprint retries 3 legacy generations (_legacy_material_ok) and explain_material_change enumerates once more = 5 full-store scans per stale child. Runtime proof via counting seam on reads.reduce_all_tickets: 6 scans for 1 child vs 21 for 4 children (RED test tests/unit/test_completion_child_gate_scan_count.py, exact 5/child slope as predicted).\n\nFIX: same remedy shape as 3d57 (commit 14aa285f963) — wrap the per-child loop in the ContextVar-scoped, lazily-built, idempotent material_child_index snapshot; every live_material_children call inside (current + legacy fingerprints + material_diff explanation) answers from one wide scan. GREEN: scans constant in child count; verdict-correctness guards (true-fingerprint child stays certified, stale child lands uncertified, unclosed child still blocks) pass. Mutation check: fix reverted -> test RED again (21 vs 6), restored -> GREEN.\n\nATTRIBUTION (differs from 3d57's caused_by cb6b-24b4-1056-4ee6 — verified, not assumed): git log -S shows commit 66f0220d747 (epic dark-acme-lumen PR #98, pre-Gerrit, no trailer) introduced BOTH halves at once — the per-child compute_validity call in _child_closure_findings AND the completion branch's material-fingerprint recompute. cb6b (dcf41e78234) only surfaced pin health and never touched this site. The story that scoped the gate migration + validity-on-read is 929e-1971-6ad5-4fad (head-relic-twine, 'Gate migration + reopen-aware completion validity'), so caused_by = 929e-1971-6ad5-4fad; class = plan_defect (the O(N) full-store cost shipped with the design of the validity-on-read gate loop, not as a later regression of working behavior... the behavior was never fast).\n\nSIBLING SWEEP (Step 7): construct sweep over compute_validity/current_material_fingerprint call sites found ONE remaining per-item loop outside a snapshot: orchestrator.delivered_children_manifest (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py:151) loops children through delivered_now -> _attested_delivered -> compute_validity('completion-verifier') per closed child. Filing as a separate ticket linked discovered_from (same pattern 3d57 used to file this bug). All other call sites are single-shot (sidecar, remediation_mode, completion_banking, opcert jobs, transition_close, verify_opcert) or already inside a snapshot (audit/read.py, derive_plan_material_pin_health).","timestamp":1787443696542368001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CLOSE EVIDENCE (2026-08-22). Fix landed on main as 37d29f017c88 (Gerrit change 2136, Change-Id Iee0f9246c2d43187494f67d3be064c6dbd5a2730, LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 via https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/32608359224, submitted via Rebase-If-Necessary).\n\nAC1 (scan count constant in child count): tests/unit/test_completion_child_gate_scan_count.py::test_child_gate_scan_count_constant_in_child_count — RED before fix (6 scans for 1 child vs 21 for 4, exactly 5/child: 1 current fingerprint + 3 legacy generations + 1 stale-material explanation), GREEN after (constant). Mutation check: fix reverted -> RED again (21 vs 6), restored -> GREEN.\nAC2 (verdicts unchanged): verdict-correctness guards pass — a child attesting its TRUE current fingerprint stays certified (not uncertified), a stale child lands in uncertified, an unclosed child still blocks deterministically. Neighbor suites green (test_pin_health_store_scan_count, test_child_closure_evidence_6ec8, test_delivered_now, test_close_disposition_attestation_738a).\nAC3 (gates): make lint (incl. complexity ratchet) + make typecheck clean; plan-review attestation certified at 264f955ff09.\n\nClass: regression (matching sibling 3d57) — container close was fast until 66f0220d747 added the per-child compute_validity + completion-branch fingerprint recompute. caused_by: 929e-1971-6ad5-4fad (head-relic-twine, the dark-acme-lumen story that scoped the gate migration + validity-on-read), passed explicitly on the close; NOT cb6b-24b4-1056-4ee6 (3d57's origin — verified it never touched this site).\n\nStep-7 sibling: bb3a-c931-47ba-4808 (dendritic-taxidermic-lovebird) filed + linked discovered_from for the remaining per-child loop in orchestrator.delivered_children_manifest. All other compute_validity/current_material_fingerprint call sites verified single-shot or already inside a snapshot.\n\nResidual (pre-existing, not mine): tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py::test_five_environment_matrix_has_identical_results_without_gh fails 5/11 params on clean origin/main on this host (confirmed with fix stashed) — environmental/pre-existing; CI is green, so likely host-specific. Not dispositioned as a ticket here; noting for the record.","timestamp":1787448539605227001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787435008109107001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f202e270-1026-4d23-bc8d-fdce81343ef5","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3d57-602f-0b75-48ee"},{"link_uuid":"5f3fa049-c06e-44e2-9cbc-e5aaa2914fa3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b987-5e5e-0761-4259"},{"link_uuid":"c59b8f34-6a99-409e-a2c5-b8f28924c0d9","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"929e-1971-6ad5-4fad"}],"description":"Sibling of bug 3d57-602f-0b75-48ee (found in its Step-7 construct sweep): the completion child-closure gate pays a full-store scan per child (and up to 5 with legacy fingerprint retries + the stale-material explanation) when closing a container.\n\n## Mechanism\n\nsrc/rebar/llm/completion_child_gate.py loops a parent's direct children and calls compute_validity(sig, c, \"completion-verifier\") per child; the completion branch (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py:568-574) recomputes current_material_fingerprint (1 full-store reduce via relation_snapshot.live_material_children -> _reads.list_tickets(parent=...)) and on mismatch tries _legacy_material_ok (3 more full computations) plus explain_material_change (1 more). A container close with N children costs O(5N) full-store scans (measured: 6 scans for 1 child, 21 for 4).\n\n## Fix\n\nSame remedy shape as bug 3d57 (commit 14aa285f963): open `with material_child_index(repo_root=repo_root):` around the per-child validity loop in completion_child_gate.py (extracted as _classify_children so the snapshot wraps exactly the loop that fingerprints). One wide scan per close instead of O(5N). Correctness precedent: the snapshot's fast path filters through counts_as_plan_material_child, byte-identical to the slow path (proven in bug 3d57; regression test tests/unit/test_pin_health_store_scan_count.py shows the counting pattern reused here).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Full-store reduce count during a container close's child-closure check does not grow with child count — proven by `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_completion_child_gate_scan_count.py::test_child_gate_scan_count_constant_in_child_count` (RED before the fix: 6 vs 21 scans; GREEN after).\n- [x] Gate verdicts unchanged: a child attesting its true current fingerprint stays certified, a stale child lands uncertified, an unclosed child still blocks — proven by `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_completion_child_gate_scan_count.py` (verdict-correctness guards).\n- [x] `make lint` + `make typecheck` + complexity ratchet (`python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`) clean.\n\n## Testing\n\nRED-first counting-seam regression test tests/unit/test_completion_child_gate_scan_count.py (mirrors tests/unit/test_pin_health_store_scan_count.py): monkeypatch-counts rebar._engine_support.reads.reduce_all_tickets, asserts scan count constant in child count, plus verdict-correctness and unclosed-child blocking guards. Mutation check: fix reverted returns the test to RED.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion_child_gate.py","reason":"open the shared material_child_index snapshot around the per-child validity loop (extracted as _classify_children)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_completion_child_gate_scan_count.py","reason":"scan-count regression test + verdict-correctness guards"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","b987-5e5e-0761-4259"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f84e77ca-534c-4dce-b3f6-79b32177b214","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a3f5-5c19-faad-417b","ticket_type":"bug","title":"completion child gate scans full store per child","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["08ceca0e-cfe0-4fda-b38d-03301db18897","36501f29-fe5c-4e1d-bd5d-c810371607ed","d5b51b5f-9d27-40cc-b0de-6fd122760d16","301c2e59-35ed-4647-b75f-60ae5d49470a","a8289a1f-6e66-44a2-8024-fb9df90a7148","5f3fa049-c06e-44e2-9cbc-e5aaa2914fa3","d32a6ca7-babc-4db5-b4a0-042ac1356dd9","f157829e-8252-48cb-8c33-a759c33ca88c","fbbd6757-c7e0-47ca-8431-c09f853ce2a2","f84e77ca-534c-4dce-b3f6-79b32177b214","c677e2f1-253a-4f4a-869c-9e2d0cbe506e","c59b8f34-6a99-409e-a2c5-b8f28924c0d9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787461476188894001,"uuid":"62d36064-b072-4763-94e2-99575957ca79"}